#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064167 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064038 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f2a4550c-7ed7-58aa-8928-23dd1cfd0cd7" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Antiderivative of a Monomial"}] :question/id #uuid "368cbbae-4eff-5eff-a8f3-d3e8359447a9" :question/math-academy-id "e-364" :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int x^2 \\,\\textrm d x$." :question/worked-solution "We apply the power rule with $n=2$, and we get\n\n$$\n\\int x^2 \\,\\textrm d x = \\dfrac{x^{2+1}}{2+1} + C = \\dfrac{x^3}{3}+C\n$$\n\nLet's check by differentiating:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{d}{dx}(\\frac{x^{3}}{3} + C) &=  \\\\\n\\frac{d}{dx}(\\frac{x^{3}}{3}) + \\frac{d}{dx}(C) &=  \\\\\n\\frac{1}{3}\\frac{d}{dx}(x^{3}) + 0 &=  \\\\\n\\frac{1}{3} \\cdot 3x^{2} &=  \\\\\n&= x^{2}✓\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f2a4550c-7ed7-58aa-8928-23dd1cfd0cd7" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048593}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064554 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f2a4550c-7ed7-58aa-8928-23dd1cfd0cd7" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Antiderivative of a Monomial"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bd9ded59-ba65-5176-b8f9-b0abbcde8e5e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061520} {:answer/id #uuid "06876c28-ebd0-5db2-80b3-e9af69ed8c2a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{2}}{2} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061521} {:answer/id #uuid "1e1c848c-bcad-5a85-903a-9791288e9010" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061522} {:answer/id #uuid "53a354ab-679e-5199-ac84-f449177db3d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061523} {:answer/id #uuid "759d2e84-4518-561f-8c74-506babc880c4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{2} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061524}] :answer-field/id #uuid "d83860ac-499e-5a75-812f-1da4dee6be22" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061519}] :question/id #uuid "9681ab06-ae34-5546-895c-3849a33f13b3" :question/math-academy-id "q-2005" :question/problem "Calculate $\\intxdx$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064556 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f2a4550c-7ed7-58aa-8928-23dd1cfd0cd7" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Antiderivative of a Monomial"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a441ddd8-cdfd-510b-9645-167a452b9e7c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{5} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061532} {:answer/id #uuid "b6abf952-05e5-525b-9306-14df3eb50611" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4x^{3} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061533} {:answer/id #uuid "b8fbde76-9228-5e56-b028-6340005dc28d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{4}}{4} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061534} {:answer/id #uuid "4e170175-65b7-57c4-b9e2-727b6b0c9179" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{5}}{5} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061535} {:answer/id #uuid "4f79a5e8-a535-5732-a68c-46578acb44dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{3} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061536}] :answer-field/id #uuid "5f64550e-ffcf-5991-a4ac-264a9e506706" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061531}] :question/id #uuid "a4162e45-b600-54a2-bad9-383dac48cede" :question/math-academy-id "q-2022" :question/problem "Calculate $\\intx^{4}dx$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233174 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f2a4550c-7ed7-58aa-8928-23dd1cfd0cd7" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Antiderivative of a Monomial"}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6e6c66f6-6133-59f6-a79d-0cbf1615accf" :question/math-academy-id "q-113665" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int {x}^{20}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "We apply the power rule with $n=20$, and we get\n\n$$\n\\int {x}^{20}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{{x}^{20+1}}{20+1}+C=\\frac{{x}^{21}}{21}+C.\n$$\n\nLet's check by differentiating:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{{x}^{21}}{21}+C) & = \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{{x}^{21}}{21})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) & = \\\\ \\frac{1}{21}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{21})+0 & = \\\\ \\frac{1}{21}\\cdot 21{x}^{20} & = \\\\ {x}^{20}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233175 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f2a4550c-7ed7-58aa-8928-23dd1cfd0cd7" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Antiderivative of a Monomial"}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7949e7bf-09d1-5ce9-ac3c-0d7f26b2e6c4" :question/math-academy-id "q-113670" :question/problem "Calculate $F(x)$ given that $f(x)={x}^{17}$ and ${F}^{'}(x)=f(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that integration is the opposite of differentiation. So, if ${F}^{'}(x)=f(x),$ then integrating both sides of this equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{F}^{'}(x) & =f(x) \\\\ \\int {F}^{'}(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ F(x) & =\\int f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe apply the power rule with $n=17$, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(x) & =\\int f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {x}^{17}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{17+1}}{17+1}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{18}}{18}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's check by differentiating:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{{x}^{18}}{18}+C) & = \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{{x}^{18}}{18})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) & = \\\\ \\frac{1}{18}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{18})+0 & = \\\\ \\frac{1}{18}\\cdot 18\\,{x}^{17} & = \\\\ {x}^{17}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186234186 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f2a4550c-7ed7-58aa-8928-23dd1cfd0cd7" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Antiderivative of a Monomial"}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "48cc16d0-0280-564d-bcf3-e481ad8d20ab" :question/math-academy-id "q-66126" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int 1\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "If we write the integrand as a power of $x$, we have ${x}^{0}=1.$ Therefore, we can use the power rule with $n=0$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 1\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {x}^{0}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{0+1}}{0+1}+C \\\\  & =x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's check by differentiating:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x+C) & = \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) & = \\\\ 1+0 & = \\\\ 1\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186234300 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f2a4550c-7ed7-58aa-8928-23dd1cfd0cd7" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Antiderivative of a Monomial"}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "eb47b292-deba-58b8-a79e-0386e8ea55e3" :question/math-academy-id "q-71121" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int {x}^{10}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "We apply the power rule with $n=10$, and we get\n\n$$\n\\int {x}^{10}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{{x}^{10+1}}{10+1}+C=\\frac{{x}^{11}}{11}+C.\n$$\n\nLet's check by differentiating:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{{x}^{11}}{11}+C) & = \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{{x}^{11}}{11})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) & = \\\\ \\frac{1}{11}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{11})+0 & = \\\\ \\frac{1}{11}\\cdot 11{x}^{10} & = \\\\ {x}^{10}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Antiderivative of a Monomial"}]}
